{"subjectId":"data-science","id":"stop-words","title":"Stop Words","group":"Natural Language Processing","order":16,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Stop words are very common words (“is”, “the”, “a”) that carry little meaning on their own. Removing them shrinks the text and highlights the words that matter.</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>from nltk.corpus import stopwords\nfrom nltk.tokenize import word_tokenize\n\nstop_words = set(stopwords.words(\"english\"))\nprint(len(stop_words), \"is\" in stop_words, \"good\" in stop_words)   # 198 True False\n\ntxt = \"This is not a good time to talk.\"\nkept = [w for w in word_tokenize(txt) if w.lower() not in stop_words and len(w) &gt;= 2]\nprint(kept)                                  # ['good', 'time', 'talk']</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Careful</div><p>“not” is a stop word in NLTK's list — so “not a good time” becomes “good time”. For sentiment analysis, removing stop words can flip the meaning; keep negations.</p></div>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-language\"></i>Stop words in spaCy</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>import spacy\nnlp = spacy.load(\"en_core_web_sm\")          # python -m spacy download en_core_web_sm\n\nprint(len(nlp.Defaults.stop_words) &gt; 300)   # True\nprint(nlp.vocab[\"is\"].is_stop, nlp.vocab[\"GFG\"].is_stop)   # True False\n\nnlp.Defaults.stop_words.add(\"i.e\")          # add your own\nnlp.vocab[\"i.e\"].is_stop = True\nnlp.Defaults.stop_words.discard(\"done\")     # or remove one\nnlp.vocab[\"done\"].is_stop = False\nprint(nlp.vocab[\"i.e\"].is_stop, nlp.vocab[\"done\"].is_stop)  # True False</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p>Change both <code>nlp.Defaults.stop_words</code> (the list) and <code>nlp.vocab[word].is_stop</code> (the flag tokens check) — spaCy keeps them separately.</p></div></section>"}